    "note": "Stable uncommitted snapshot evidence proves that the exact pinned public Pub/Sub image is acquired with an isolated anonymous Docker configuration against the active daemon, then validated for immutable digest syntax, linux/amd64 platform execution (including emulation where available), and advertised --data-dir capability. Cloud Storage buckets and objects use a profile-scoped host runtime bind mount and survive exact-owned emulator-container replacement. Official Pub/Sub topics, subscriptions, and queued messages survive a MiniSky process crash/restart only while the same exact-owned Pub/Sub container remains alive; replacement loses all three. Exact-owned cleanup passed. Public registry/network access remains required, the global unowned image cache may retain an authorized pull, Pub/Sub remains amd64/emulation/session-only, and five unrelated local volumes plus a pre-existing lock observed during certification are not product evidence. Storage and Pub/Sub runtime data remain outside metadata export/import; no exactly-once, portable export, IAM, HA, security, or full-parity claim is made.",
